spoint editor 2026-06-07: user reported scene-click select dead, Place no-op, cannot move items, panel select dead, HookFlow inoperable, player still shoots in editor. Live-witnessed (localhost:8090 ?singleplayer&world=tps-game) root causes + fixes (commit on main): (1) SCENE-CLICK SELECT was the central bug: EntityLoader.js routed ModelPool entities into entityMeshes by reading modelPool._entities.get(id).root SYNCHRONOUSLY right after the ASYNC modelPool.spawn() — capturing an EMPTY anchor (env-sillos was Object3D with 0 children, witnessed). pickEntity (editor.js:135) raycasts entityMeshes filtered by userData.isEditable; raycast returned 0 hits so clicking the map selected nothing AND the gizmo had nothing to attach -> also explains cannot-move (gizmo gated on selection). FIX: inside the spawn callback set entityMeshes.set(entityId, root) when the real geometry arrives, + re-set on every lod-changed (both env and non-env branches) so LOD swaps keep the pick set live. Witnessed env-sillos 0->96 mesh descendants, raycast 0->1, pointer click selects, gizmo attaches, gizmo drag sends EDITOR_UPDATE 0x80. (2) HOOKFLOW always-empty = THREE stacked bugs: HookFlowViewer.js buildGraph filtered e._appName||e.appName only (map/gamedef carry no appName via AppRuntime.getSceneGraph:196 appName:e._appName which is undefined for stage entities); EditorShell.js updateScene set _entities + updated hierarchy but did NOT call hfViewer.updateGraph so async SCENE_GRAPH arrival never refreshed the graph; and the kit C.Table (anentrypoint-design@0.0.197) threw "i.map is not a function" inside 247420.js the moment nodes existed, killing the ENTIRE HookFlow render (the empty-state 0-node path skipped C.Table so it never threw before — masked until a real scene). FIX: relax filter to e&&e.id with kind fallback (model/primitive/entity), call hfViewer.updateGraph from updateScene, wrap C.Table in try/catch to degrade to the SVG graph on kit API drift. Witnessed 2 nodes, "2 app entities", node click selects. (3) SHOOT IN EDITOR: app.js:359-362 fed the RAW input to ams.dispatchInput (app-module onInput) while only client.sendInput got the neutralized all-false input, so a client-side weapon module could still fire visually. FIX: compute neutralized input FIRST, feed the same object to both ams.dispatchInput and client.sendInput. Witnessed no shoot reaches app modules or network in editor. (4) PLACE works (PLACE_APP 0x83 sent, entityMeshes 2->3) - the perceived no-op was the empty-anchor render race (now fixed) + only environment/tps-game apps listed. (5) panel select works on .ds-ep-tree-label (not row container). WITNESS TRAP: ES modules are CACHED - after an edit, soft reload reuses the old module; force fresh via goto(about:blank) then goto(URL), verify served file via fetch(path,{cache:no-store}); the real client mount is /editor/X.js NOT /client/editor/X.js (client/ mounted at root). Reusable harness: .claude/workflows/editor-assert.js asserts all 6 interactions. EXTENDS [[editor-select-works-rowlabel-not-container]] and [[editor-pointer-input]].